{
  "id": "proj-plyometric-jump-box",
  "slug": "plyometric-jump-box",
  "status": "published",
  "title": "Plyometric Jump Box",
  "summary": "A 3-in-1 box (20/24/30 in) cut from one sheet of plywood, glued and screwed over internal cleats so it does not wobble.",
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "estimatedHours": 3,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "Using a straight-edge guide, cut the sheet into two 24 x 30 in sides, two 20 x 30 in sides and two 20 x 24 in ends; the box stands 20, 24 or 30 in tall depending on which face is down.",
    "Mark a 1 1/4 x 5 in hand hole centred near the top of the two 24 x 30 in panels, drill a 1 in hole at each end, and cut between them with the jigsaw.",
    "Cut the 2x2s into four 28 1/2 in corner cleats and glue and screw one along each long edge of the two 20 x 30 in panels.",
    "Stand the panels up, glue the 24 x 30 in panels onto the cleats and screw through them every 6 in, then glue and screw on the two end panels.",
    "Check every face is flat on the floor, sand the edges and round them over, and wipe on two coats of polyurethane.",
    "Stick a strip of grip tape across each face you will land on."
  ],
